codex
**READY for the isolated 66-call probe**, subject to the sender’s own preflight checks passing immediately before dispatch.

The previous blockers are addressed in the final files. I verified the 16 registered hashes and reconstructed all 11 selected requests against the manifest. The independent score check passed for **13 query lists**, including the multi-query cases, and caught its vector, score, origin, candidate and missing-input mutations. The separate census matched **185 archived requests and answers**. [Registration and send gates](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/probe_send.py:49), [score check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/independent_check.py:6).

The sender now uses a single-attempt transport, journals dispatch before calling Jev, stops on failure and refuses to reuse an existing run directory. The integration test exercises that actual path with a fake lost reply and checks for one attempt, an ambiguous event and restart refusal. [Integration test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/integration_check.py:13). I inspected that test but did not run it because it creates temporary files; the live sender runs it as a required preflight.

The result will remain a **selected-case diagnostic**. C versus T measures the combined effect of adding scores and query-type labels; it cannot establish why Jev changed a decision or estimate production accuracy. The pre-outcome blind packets contain the full candidate sets with shuffled order and no scores or model decisions. The planned independent source review is still needed before judging whether changes are correct. [Blind packet construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/make_blind.py:9).

No files were edited and no paid calls were made.
